<title>SWEDEN: Skandia posts flat 1996 operating profit.</title>
<headline>Skandia posts flat 1996 operating profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurer Skandia Insurance Co Ltd posted its earnings for 1996 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			2,392   vs   2,378</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			  1,649   vs   1,551</p>
<p> Total premiums			 58,791   vs  50,731</p>
<p> Net asset value			17,856   vs  16,249</p>
<p> Net asset value per share (SKR)     174   vs     159</p>
<p> Proposed dividend per share (SKR)  2.75   vs    2.00</p>
<p>Operating profit of unit linked,</p>
<p>     life assurance operations     1,522   vs   1,078</p>
<p>Operating profit, non-life</p>
<p>     insurance and reinsurance     3,519   vs   2,278</p>
<p> Net investment income		 3,116   vs   1,207</p>
<p> Technical result			  403   vs   1,071</p>
<p> Other activities			   26   vs	14</p>
<p> Other expenses			  1,275   vs     992</p>
<p> Restructuring costs		   1,400   vs	 0</p>
<p> Tax				CHARGE   392   vs	95 CREDIT</p>
<p> Minorites				   117   vs	54</p>
<p> Net profit				1,140   vs   1,592</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	    11   vs	16</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll found market expectations for Skandia to post a pre-tax profit of 3.06 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
